---
/*
 * TEMPLATE DOCUMENT — must be reviewed by a UK solicitor before launch.
 * See README.md ("Before you go live") for the full list of legal follow-ups.
 */
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../../config';
---

<Legal
  title="Terms & Conditions"
  description={`The terms governing the supply of research materials by ${site.company.legalName}.`}
  updated="August 2026"
>
  <p class="lede">
    These terms govern the supply of products by {site.company.legalName} (&ldquo;we&rdquo;,
    &ldquo;us&rdquo;) to you. Placing an order means you accept them, together with our
    <a href="/legal/disclaimer">Research Use Disclaimer</a>, which forms part of these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>1. About us</h2>
  <p>
    {site.company.legalName} is a company registered in England and Wales
    {site.company.companyNumber !== 'TBC' && ` under number ${site.company.companyNumber}`}. You can
    reach us at <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Eligibility</h2>
  <p>
    You may only order from us if you are aged {site.minimumAge} or over and are acting as, or on
    behalf of, a qualified researcher, laboratory, institution or business. We do not knowingly
    supply consumers purchasing for personal use, and we reserve the right to request evidence of
    research capacity before accepting an order.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Orders and enquiries</h2>
  <p>
    Our website is a catalogue, not an automated checkout. Submitting an enquiry is an invitation to
    treat and does not create a contract. A contract is formed only when we confirm your order in
    writing and, where payment is due in advance, receive cleared funds.
  </p>
  <p>
    We may decline any enquiry at our discretion. Product availability is not guaranteed until
    confirmed, and batch details may change between enquiry and confirmation.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Prices and payment</h2>
  <p>
    Prices shown on the website exclude VAT and shipping, and are subject to change without notice.
    The price that applies is the one quoted in our written order confirmation.
  </p>
  <p>
    Payment is due in full before dispatch unless we have agreed account terms with you in writing.
    Where account terms apply, invoices are payable within 30 days of the invoice date, and we
    reserve the right to charge statutory interest on overdue sums under the Late Payment of
    Commercial Debts (Interest) Act 1998.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Delivery</h2>
  <p>
    We dispatch within the United Kingdom only. Delivery estimates are estimates, not guarantees,
    and we are not liable for delays caused by carriers or events outside our reasonable control.
    Risk in the products passes to you on delivery; title passes on receipt of payment in full.
  </p>
  <p>See our <a href="/legal/shipping-returns">Shipping &amp; Returns</a> page for the detail.</p>

  <h2>6. Specification and certificates</h2>
  <p>
    Each batch is supplied with a certificate of analysis stating its purity and identity as
    determined by an independent laboratory. Our obligation is to supply material conforming to the
    specification on that certificate. Where the certificate for the batch you receive differs from
    a specification quoted on the website, the certificate governs.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Your obligations</h2>
  <p>
    The obligations set out in our <a href="/legal/disclaimer">Research Use Disclaimer</a> —
    including the restriction to in-vitro laboratory research and the prohibition on administration
    to humans or animals — are incorporated into these terms and are conditions of supply. Breach of
    them entitles us to terminate supply immediately.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Liability</h2>
  <p>
    We are not liable to you for any loss of profit, loss of business, business interruption, loss
    of data, or any indirect or consequential loss. Our total liability arising from or in
    connection with any order is limited to the price paid for the products giving rise to the
    claim.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing in these terms excludes or limits our liability for death or personal injury caused by
    our negligence, for fraud or fraudulent misrepresentation, for breach of the terms implied by
    section 12 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979, or for any other liability that cannot lawfully be
    excluded or limited.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Force majeure</h2>
  <p>
    We are not liable for any failure or delay in performing our obligations where that failure or
    delay results from events outside our reasonable control.
  </p>

  <h2>10. General</h2>
  <p>
    If any provision of these terms is found to be unenforceable, the remaining provisions continue
    in force. Our failure to enforce any right is not a waiver of it. No third party has any right
    to enforce these terms under the Contracts (Rights of Third Parties) Act 1999.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms and any dispute arising out of them are governed by the laws of England and Wales,
    and are subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of England and Wales.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may amend these terms from time to time. The version in force is the one published on this
    page at the date your order is confirmed.
  </p>
</Legal>
